{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792774535,"nonce":"AVr4LVZyzzUqdcA9pQ7HsJAC5OE=","title":"Interaction makes eight signals per element eagerly; most are never read reactively","message":"From the census on d106687: every element that gets an Interaction (a :hover rule matching it is enough) creates eight SignalBool at once: hovered, pressed, focused, focusVisible, focusWithin, disabled, checked and indeterminate. Each is a finalizable native handle that the collector charges 4 KiB for, so a styled interactive div carries about 32 KB of pressure charge for state nobody follows, and a build makes eight native calls more than it needs.\n\n**What is wanted**\n\nThe Bool is the state; a signal is made the first time something reads it reactively (a getter), and the writers (Pointer, Focus, Select, Input, Toggle...) set the Bool and the signal if there is one. The non-reactive reads (`.disabled.get()` in Pointer on every event, in Focus and Keyboard) become Bool reads, so they do not make the signal either. About 60 call sites. Measure with the census scene (a div with a :hover rule, 1,000 of them): SignalBool should fall from 8 per element to 0 to 2.","files":null}]}